Terminals and DEX aggregators solve the data problem — they display prices,
charts,
liquidity,
and routes — but they do not solve the context problem. The signal still originates on social media (X, Telegram, Discord),
and the trader must manually leave that environment, open a terminal or aggregator, paste the contract address, and then execute.
The core failure is architectural:
data aggregation is not the same as execution within the signal feed — which is what AGNT Hub aims to solve.

